# Panel 180 R5, shape 111 of the compiler-engineer's 117 (extern member
# params): a break before , after a mark.
# By the spec's opening paragraph, the line ends with `n`, a name, so it keeps
# its NEWLINE, which may stand before a `,`, and in a list the two are one
# separator: accepted, exit 0.
extern "m.h"
    function g(p: ptr counted_by n
        , n: u64)

function shape()
    print(1)
